      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "After a disappointing experience with the installer who originally fitted my solar panels three years ago, which I initially considered using the same company for my solar battery installation to keep everything under one provider, I decided to explore other options.Following an initial call with a Level electrical representative and sending my electrical for the last few months, I was scheduled an appointment with electrical designer Amir. He provided me with a much better package, helped rationalise my purchase based on my actual needs, and offered clear, sensible advice.On installation day, everything went according to plan. When I had a question, Amir personally called to explain things in detail. The communication throughout the installation was excellent, and the work was carried out neatly and professionally.The follow-up after installation has also been outstanding, with remote monitoring support and practical advice on balancing my energy usage.Initially, I was hesitant to sign up with Level Electrical given the limited reviews available on SolarQuotes, but I can honestly say I am very pleasantly surprised and impressed so far.In contrast, my original installer, EISS, showed little to no planning for the system at all and I felt was favoured for asking questions. They took an instalment payment in mid-May for a July installation (with the rebate), held onto the money for few weeks, then eventually returned it after saying they weren’t sure about the system. Later, when I approached them again, they had no issue to install the very same system they had rejected—this time with an extra $2,000 added, saying: “Sorry mate, prices have increased.”",
